cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this Lean formalization, please cite it using this metadata, and cite the paper it formalizes (listed under references)."
title: "bernoulli-perron-variational: variational properties of Perron's extremal solutions in the Bernoulli one-phase problem, in Lean"
version: "0.1.0"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/willmfeldman/bernoulli-perron-variational"
authors:
  - family-names: Feldman
    given-names: "William M."
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Abedin, Feldman and Stinson, "Variational properties of
  Perron's extremal solutions in the Bernoulli one-phase problem" (arXiv:2609.14981). For the
  one-phase Bernoulli problem with a Lipschitz coefficient on a bounded C² domain, Perron's
  smallest supersolution and largest subsolution are viscosity solutions, inner variational
  solutions, and one-sided minimizers of the Alt–Caffarelli energy near every free boundary
  point. In the plane, the largest subsolution is classical, and the smallest supersolution is
  classical off a set where every blow-up is a two-plane solution. The proof goes through a
  semilinear parabolic approximation, its singular limit, and the long-time limit.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formalized mathematics
  - free boundary problems
  - Bernoulli problem
  - one-phase problem
  - Perron's method
  - viscosity solutions
  - inner variational solutions
